# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

This project was created by Labframe. The starter is a complete Rabi-flop example: QuTiP produces saved numerical data, lmfit fits those saved data, Matplotlib creates a combined figure, and the summary hook writes Markdown and HTML reports plus a project home page for all runs.

## Smoke test

From this directory:

```bash
uv run labframe run --no-commit configs/smoke.yaml
```

If this project is managed by Poetry and Labframe was added from its local checkout with `poetry add /path/to/labframe`, use:

```bash
poetry run labframe run --no-commit configs/smoke.yaml
```

The smoke configuration is intentionally small and `--no-commit` requires a clean working tree. Always pass `configs/smoke.yaml` explicitly during automated validation; omitting the configuration selects `configs/default.yaml`.

## Project files

```text
configs/           YAML run configurations
.labframe.yaml     Run-artifact directory and default Git commit settings
runs/              Default run-artifact directory (ignored by Git)
index.html         Generated run home page (created after the first run and ignored by Git)
simulation.py      Simulation dispatch, saved results, and fitting examples
fit_models.py      Reusable lmfit model objects
plot_results.py    Figures built from saved results
build_summary.py   Markdown and HTML built from saved artifacts
pyproject.toml     Standalone dependencies; omitted by `labframe init --no-venv`
```

The starter's `simulation.py` saves `rabi_flop.npz`, reads it back for fitting, and saves a densely sampled `rabi_flop_fit.npz`. Plotting and summary generation consume those files without rerunning the simulation.

## Run output

Every invocation creates `<runs-dir>/<timestamp>_<config-hash>/`, where `<runs-dir>` is configured in `.labframe.yaml` and defaults to `runs/`:

```text
config.yaml
meta.json
output.log
results/
figures/
summary.md
summary.html
```

After a successful run, the summary hook also rebuilds `index.html` in the project root, including when the configured run directory is outside the project. Open it directly in a browser to view every run that has a `summary.html`, grouped by the configured run type. Each per-run HTML summary links back to this home page.

For normal work, copy or edit a configuration and run it explicitly:

```bash
uv run labframe run configs/my-run.yaml
```

For a Poetry-managed project, the equivalent command is:

```bash
poetry run labframe run configs/my-run.yaml
```

`.labframe.yaml` also controls the default commit mode for `labframe run`:

```yaml
runs_dir: runs
commit: true
```

Set `commit: false` to make clean, no-commit runs the project default. Use `--commit` or `--no-commit` to override it for one invocation. Commit mode records the source state used at launch and commits changed launch source only after the run succeeds. Completed run folders are immutable records and should not be edited.

## Customize

- Keep simulation or acquisition output in the supplied `results/` directory.
- Configure fit parameter values, bounds, and `vary` explicitly in `simulation.py`; do not use model guesses.
- Keep reusable model objects in `fit_models.py`.
- Build plots from `results/` and write them to `figures/`.
- Build summaries and the run index from saved artifacts only.
